<title>CANADA: DBRS confirms Empire ratings.</title>
<headline>DBRS confirms Empire ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominion Bond Rating Service said on Monday it confirmed the ratings for Empire Co's debentures at A (low) and its preferred shares at Pfd-2, both with a negative trend.</p>
<p>The rating agency also confirmed Empire's commercial paper at R-1 (low) with a stable trend.</p>
<p>DBRS said the price war with Loblaw Cos continues to affect earnings at Empire's Sobeys retail unit. The company's investment portfolio has continued to increase in value, which has improved debt coverage ratios, DBRS said.</p>
<p>Empire remained dependent on the mature, slow growth economy of Atlantic Canada but is starting to diversify earnings with expansion into Quebec, DBRS said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
